On 6/26/07, m.kornig@sondal.net <m.kornig@sondal.net> wrote:
>
> So it's {mi'e tim} (no article) and {mi'e la
> djein. e la tim} (articles needed in front of both
> names)?

Yes, those are both valid, and so is {mi'e la tim}.

{mi'e}, and all other members of selma'o COI, can be followed by:

(1) a cmevla or series of cmevla: {mi'e tim}, {mi'e tim tam tum}, etc.

(2) a selbri: {mi'e pendo}, {mi'e pendo be do}, etc.

(3) a sumti (including connected sumti): {mi'e la tim}, {mi'e la tim e
la djein},
{mi'e le klama}, {mi'e mi}, {mi'e da}, {mi'e zo mi'e}, {mi'e lu dei
jufra li'u}, etc.

(4) the terminator {do'u}: {mi'e do'u}.

In addition, relative clauses can be inserted before or after the cmevla
or selbri (a sumti already allows for relative clauses).

mu'o mi'e xorxes


